.TH SSHUSH 1 "2026" "sshush" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sshush \- interactive terminal UI for SSH keys, the agent, and ssh_config
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sshush
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sshush
is an interactive terminal UI for managing SSH keys, the ssh-agent, and your
.IR ~/.ssh/config :
switch keys, see what is loaded in the agent, browse hosts, and edit the config
without leaving the terminal.
.PP
Run with no arguments to launch the interactive UI. Config edits are gated behind
a confirmation and a
.I .bak
backup is written before the first change of a session.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B load-default
Load the configured default identities into the agent and exit. Intended for
shell startup files (see
.BR shell-init ).
.TP
.B shell-init
Print a shell snippet that loads the default identities on shell start. Append it
to your shell rc, e.g.
.IR ~/.bashrc " or " ~/.zshrc .
.TP
.B restore
Revert the SSH config (and any Included files) to the
.I .bak
snapshot written before sshush's first edit of the session.
.TP
.B update
Update sshush to the latest release in place. Only available for released builds.
.TP
.B version
Print the installed version.
.TP
.B "completion " \fIshell\fR
Print a shell completion script for
.IR bash ", " zsh ", or " fish .
.TP
.B install-extras
Install the man page and shell completions to user-level directories. With
.B \-\-refresh
only files that already exist are updated (used by
.B update
after a binary swap).
.TP
.B help
Show usage.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
In the interactive UI: arrow keys or
.IR k / j
move,
.I tab
switches panes,
.I /
filters,
.I enter
loads a key or connects to a host,
.I n / d
create or delete,
.I e
edits a host,
.I i
attaches keys,
.I R
restores from backup,
.I t / m
switch theme or toggle motion, and
.I ?
shows the full keybinding reference. Press
.I q
to quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.ssh/config
The SSH client configuration sshush reads and edits (following
.B Include
directives).
.TP
.I ~/.config/sshush/config.toml
sshush's own settings: default identities, SSH dir/config overrides, color theme,
and motion preferences.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SSH_AUTH_SOCK
The ssh-agent socket used for agent features.
.TP
.B SSHUSH_SSH_DIR
Override the SSH directory (default
.IR ~/.ssh ).
.TP
.B SSHUSH_CONFIG
Override the SSH config file path.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colored output.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh-add (1),
.BR ssh-keygen (1),
.BR ssh_config (5)
